    "text": "<p>Siderite<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>FeCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Siderite is a mineral composed of iron (II) carbonate (FeCO<sub>3</sub>). It is a widespread mineral that is an ore of iron.&nbsp;</p><p>Calamine<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>ZnCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Zinc ore is most commonly found as zinc carbonate&nbsp;(ZnCO<sub>3</sub>â€‹), known as calamine or smithsonite.&nbsp;</p><p>Kaolinite<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi>Si</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math></p><p>Malachite<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi>CuCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p>",
